** TODO The test driver's generator has the three departures the library's had

=tests/src/rand.cpp= carries the subtractive generator of
=src/random.cpp= twice, in 32-bit and in 64-bit words (=rw_seed32=
44-68, =rw_seed64= 94-118), with the three departures the library's
had: the second index starts 35 slots ahead of the first, where lags
55 and 24 put it 31 ahead; the seeding loop never writes slot 34; the
warm-up loop indexes ~[i]~ inside the loop over =ii=. In the
library's the low bit of the output repeated every 7665 draws; this
copy is read, not measured. =23.bitset= is its one user and draws
that bit, ~rw_rand (2U)~ at 88. Seen while the library's generator
was corrected, 2026-11-15.

Fix: the three corrections of =src/random.cpp=, in both widths; then
=23.bitset='s count is read against its pin.

Check: the low bit of 2^20 draws of =rw_rand32= has no period.

