** TODO Ten tests build with warnings of their own

GCC 16 in 15D warns on the sources of eight container tests and two
=valarray= ones, apart from what the library's headers draw:

- =-Wunused-local-typedefs=: =23.bitset.cons= 295 (=String=),
  =23.list.assign= 278 and 280, =23.list.capacity= 307,
  =23.list.cons= 397 and 641, =23.list.erase= 275 (=ListIter=,
  =ListState=), =23.vector.modifiers= 1054 to 1056.
- =-Wshadow=: =23.vector.modifiers= 717, a local =Vector= over the
  global one.
- =-Wcatch-value=: =23.vector.capacity= 137 catches
  =std::length_error= by value.
- =23.vector.stdcxx-494= 49: an =operator new= that returns null
  without ~throw ()~.
- =-Wsized-deallocation=: =26.valarray.members.stdcxx-313= and
  =26.valarray.unary.stdcxx-314= replace =operator delete= without
  the sized form.

Hypothesis: the rest of the suite has more of each; only the list,
vector, bitset and =valarray= tests were built and read. Seen while the
Containers entries were closed, 2026-11-14.

Fix: the unused typedefs leave, the catch takes a reference, the
local takes another name; the replaced =operator new= and =operator
delete= are the regression tests' subjects and are read before they
are touched.

Check: the list, vector, bitset and =valarray= tests build in 15D
with no warning that names a file under =tests=.

