(measured 2026-11-16, 11S); under GCC it is an error. The pure
=_cstring.h= declares the pairs itself (58-97). Seen while
=ref-c-headers.md= was written.

Fix: with the entry above: the const-correct pair in =std= for a
compiler without glibc's, behind a characterization; or the pure
model for =eccp= ("The pure C headers").

